module

public import Degenne2023Existence.D2023.Setting
public import Degenne2023Existence.ForLMLExplore.Probability.LargeDeviations.Cramer

/-!
# Lemma 11 of [D23]: the large deviation principle of the empirical mean

The empirical mean of `n` independent samples of the member of mean `μ` of a one-parameter
canonical exponential family, generated by a nonzero measure, satisfies the large deviation
principle with speed `n` and good rate function `x ↦ KL(x, μ)`: Cramér's theorem for exponential
families. The rate function is the divergence `d(x, μ)` of the family at its means `x`, extended
to every level by the Cramér rate function of the member of mean `μ` (`Measure.expFamilyRate`).

## Main statements

* `Degenne2023Existence.isLDP_empiricalMean_expFamily`: [D23, Lemma 11].

## References

* [D23] R. Degenne, *On the existence of a complexity in fixed budget bandit identification*,
  COLT 2023, arXiv:2303.09468v2.
-/

@[expose] public section

open MeasureTheory LMLExplore

namespace Degenne2023Existence

/-- **Cramér's theorem for exponential families** [D23, Lemma 11]. For a nonzero measure `ρ` on
`ℝ` and a mean `μ` of the exponential family generated by `ρ` with the statistic `id`, the laws of
the empirical means `(∑ i < n, X i) / n` of `n` independent samples of the member of mean `μ`
satisfy the large deviation principle with speed `n` and good rate function `x ↦ KL(x, μ)`, the
Cramér rate function `ρ.expFamilyRate id x μ` of the member of mean `μ`.

The hypothesis `NeZero ρ` is implicit in [D23], whose families are families of probability
measures: for `ρ = 0` the only mean is `0`, its member is the zero measure, and the lower bound of
the principle fails (`notes/statement-corrections.md`). -/
theorem isLDP_empiricalMean_expFamily {ρ : Measure ℝ} [NeZero ρ] {μ : ℝ}
    (hμ : μ ∈ ρ.expFamilyMeans id) :
    IsLDP (fun n ↦ (Measure.pi fun _ : Fin n ↦ ρ.expFamily id (ρ.natParam id μ)).map
        fun x : Fin n → ℝ ↦ (∑ i, x i) / (n : ℝ)) (fun x ↦ ρ.expFamilyRate id x μ) ∧
      IsGoodRateFunction (fun x ↦ ρ.expFamilyRate id x μ) :=
  isLDP_cramer_expFamily hμ

end Degenne2023Existence
